  "comment": "One fixture for board.BacklogOrder (Go) and backlogboard.backlogList (TS): the same cards in the same board order must read in the same backlog order. `cards` is the board in its order; `wire` is what the server sends a client for each backlog card (status.lineage as uid/type pairs) - pkg/apiserver checks it against CardResource, so the client's input is the server's own answer; `order` is the backlog of team alpha as both sides read it; `subtask` is which cards ride a parent TASK (board.IsSubtask / subtasks.isSubtask) - a review card's own stray parent naming a plan item makes it no subtask, so a taken one stays on the day boards. The order is the board's (Q2, docs/design/ordering.md): the reviews nobody has taken first, then the tasks, each by its own key.",
